    "survey": "Inner Mission North Context Statement, adopted 2004",
    "source": "inner-mission-north-context-statement",
    "district": "South Van Ness Avenue–Shotwell–Folsom Streets (SVN-S-F); Inner Mission Commercial Corridor",
    "status": "Contributor",
    "note": "Contributor to the South Van Ness Avenue–Shotwell–Folsom Streets (SVN-S-F) California Register eligible district (423-433 South Van Ness). Criterion A: an isolated pocket of pre-1906 buildings left unharmed by the earthquake and fire, near a larger surviving group at 573 South Van Ness Avenue. Integrity is moderate; the survey says the district is not likely to qualify for the National Register. Contributor to the Inner Mission Commercial Corridor locally significant area (423-433 South Van Ness). Formerly called the 16th Street Commercial Corridor. Criterion C: San Francisco's largest concentration of residential-over-commercial and small-scale commercial buildings, spanning both pre-1906 and post-disaster construction, dated c. 1870s–1931."
